    description: "Dart hashed signature: named-parameter names are not hashed, while non-type words are.\n\n1. OWNER DECISION. A Dart named parameter's name is visible to callers but not hashed: f({int a}) and f({int b}) share an id. Same question as Swift argument labels (WI-lonoh's labels part, owner-ruled to the final v17 PR).\n2. Words that are not types stay in the hashed text: final, var, const, covariant and annotations. f(final int x) and f(int x) hash apart; f(var x) and f(x) hash apart.\n3. Dart records keep positional field names: (int a, int b) and (int x, int y) hash apart (positional record field names are documentation only).\nState after PR 3 commit 2217d7f4a (_dart_hashed_signature renders from the syntax tree). All move ids: candidates for the final v17 PR. Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr3/agent8/RESULTS.md R2-R4."  # c20f
